WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
A bakery can bake 5,000 loaves a week.

2
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.710
This week it bakes only 2,500.

3
00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.430
The rent and the ovens
cost the same either way,

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.160
so each loaf carries a big share.

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.850
Half empty sounds like bad news.

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.240
So surely the goal is
to run at 100 per cent?

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.930
Yet many firms aim a little below.

8
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.330
So why can a factory working flat out be

9
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:26.550
just as worrying as one
standing half empty?

10
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:30.080
In this mission, you'll measure
capacity utilisation and watch

11
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.320
costs move in a graph lab.

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.240
Then you'll meet lean production:

13
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.700
quality, Kaizen and just-in-time,
and one car maker's warning

14
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.990
about a single missing part.

15
00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:43.910
Your mission: explain
what can go wrong at both

16
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.010
ends of the gauge.
